# What ships in the VSIX: package.json, README.md, LICENSE, SECURITY.md,
# docs/icon.png and out/**. The authority on that list is
# scripts/vsix-manifest.txt, which scripts/smoke-vsix.sh diffs against the built
# archive -- read that, not this file, for what actually ships.
#
# node_modules is not listed here, and this file used to claim that was fine
# because "vsce packages zero node_modules entries, and they are
# devDependencies". The second half is true and the first half is not a
# guarantee it buys. MEASURED, 29 August 2026: with 58 packages present in
# node_modules that are in neither package.json nor package-lock.json -- left
# behind by an `npm install` on another branch -- `npx vsce ls` lists 3,690
# node_modules paths and `vsce package` puts every one of them in the archive.
#
# So what keeps node_modules out is not this file and not a property of vsce.
# It is node_modules containing nothing but the devDependencies vsce skips,
# which is what `npm ci` produces and what an `npm install` on a branch with
# extra dependencies does not. The check that catches the difference is
# scripts/smoke-vsix.sh, because it reads the archive; `vsce ls` sees it too.
# Neither runs automatically. See docs/ROADMAP.md, 0.1.2.
#
# out/ is also required in full: hooks.ts resolves out/cli.js from
# context.extensionPath to install the pre-commit hook. Note that out/ is a
# denylist entry's blind spot: any artifact another branch leaves there -- an
# out/mcp.js, say -- is admitted by default. `vscode:prepublish` runs
# `npm run clean` before `npm run bundle`, so a real package or publish starts
# from an empty out/ and cannot ship one; `vsce ls` does NOT run prepublish and
# will list whatever is on disk. The manifest diff is what catches the rest.

# Development sources — only the compiled output in out/ is executed.
src/**
tests/**

# The changelog.
#
# OPEN DECISION, deliberately left excluded. The Marketplace renders CHANGELOG.md
# on the extension's listing page, and many extensions ship it on purpose. It is
# excluded here only because it arrived mid-release and shipping it would have
# been a side effect of adding a file rather than a choice anyone made. Including
# it is a one-line change plus a scripts/vsix-manifest.txt update; the decision
# belongs to whoever publishes, not to the commit that wrote the file.
CHANGELOG.md

# The detection benchmark. Generators, labels and a scorer -- development
# tooling with no runtime role, and it plants credential-shaped values.
bench/**

# Prose that belongs in the repository, not in the extension. Listed before it
# exists on purpose: this file has already shipped two things nobody meant to
# send (tsconfig.tests.json and an npm tarball) purely because a denylist
# includes anything new by default.
docs/**

# ...except the Marketplace icon, which package.json points at. Without this
# line `vsce package` refuses to build at all — "The specified icon
# 'extension/docs/icon.png' wasn't found in the extension" — so the negation is
# what makes an icon under docs/ usable, not a nicety. (`vsce ls` is the quiet
# one: it simply omits the icon and reports nothing, which is why the listing
# alone is not a check.) Verified that nothing else returns through this
# negation: src/ and tests/ still contribute zero entries.
!docs/icon.png

# Build configuration and repository tooling. scripts/ holds the release gate
# that packs and runs the npm tarball; it is never loaded by the extension.
scripts/**
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.tests.json
.npmignore
.github/**
.gitignore
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**

# Source maps: useful when debugging locally, dead weight in a published VSIX.
out/**/*.map

# Scan reports. A SecretLoop run in the repo root leaves results.sarif behind,
# and a VSIX built straight afterwards shipped it — 74 kB of findings, including
# every value the report quotes. Denylists include anything new by default,
# which is exactly how this got into a package listing unnoticed.
*.sarif

# Local validation and coverage artifacts, if any are ever produced here.
*.py
coverage/**
.nyc_output/**

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Config template — documentation, not runtime input. The extension reads a
# real .secretloop.json from the user's own workspace, never from the VSIX.
.secretloop.example.json

# Previously built packages. *.tgz matters as much as *.vsix: `npm pack` before
# `vsce package` is the ordinary release order, and without it the npm tarball
# was packaged inside the extension.
*.vsix
*.tgz

